Z||000000||eastex87gt||08-05-2001||01:15 PM||||I have bought my kevlar clutch and am ready to begin.  Is there a way lower the engine without discharging the Air Conditioner.  Thanks people.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-05-2001||01:31 PM||||Remove the compressor from its mount and hang it out of the way, like you would a caliper.||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-05-2001||02:43 PM||||I agree with Indiana.But just to let you know I have changed tranny in my garage and was able to lower the cradle enough with out disconnecting any major components.Such as water pump hoses ,a/c. compressor or hoses that go to it.maybe I got lucky ?||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||08-05-2001||02:59 PM||||You might want to read "How to remove the transaxle" at Ed Park's website: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#trany" TARGET=_blank>Rock The Cradle</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||JayUSA77||08-05-2001||03:07 PM||||just so you know. in my 4cyl when i changed the clutch it wasnt possible to take out the transaxle. I had extremely poor access to the clutch about 4 inches and i barely changed in. The only problems with that is you have to be careful when tighting the bolts to loose. (Because torque wrench couldnt fit.) in any case good luck. And email me at jayusa77@home.com if you want me to send you the chiltons section on how to remove transaxle.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
